  "summary": "Malicious code in aurenatts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (5869d16450da25408cefa75ae7be59ed27dd99952bf7161b655f6be6289dcaa5)\nNo evidence of exfiltration, install-time remote code execution, silent-relay, credential distribution, backdoor, or self-propagation was observed in this package version. No lifecycle hooks, outbound network calls to attacker-controlled destinations, credential-path reads, or obfuscated payloads were identified in the scanned files.\n\n## Source: kam193 (ecc8915a04d9fbab4ecc0437f5eb05357d2e63bc3d30f629d67c7b3eb2c98eeb)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
